forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:30:19-07:00","id":909367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/890471-what-is-your-god-machine-truth-why-is-it-doing-the-things-it-does?p=909229#post909229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Y'know, this is such an obvious Hell for a relatively unambitious Tempter... Set up shop in a time splinter and make it your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to work more on that alt-&quot;history&quot; shard I have cooking. It's basically the &quot;take over Time-Splinter&quot; concept writ large (and expanded into a patchwork alternate world &quot;fantasy&quot; setting) by a Ring of Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T13:54:57-07:00","id":909456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/890471-what-is-your-god-machine-truth-why-is-it-doing-the-things-it-does?p=899071#post899071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, by doing so you are (if you're a demon) writing yourself out of reality because the thing that created you never existed. If not, you're still creating a temporal paradox, because if the GM never existed, how would you know to go back in time and destroy it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly according to Mage, temporal paradoxes aren't a thing. Think Corridors of Time for a moment - every time you use it, it ought to cause a &quot;temporal paradox&quot; because you are going back in time to change your own history, which negates the need to go back in time.<br /> <br /> And technically from a logical standpoint, temporal paradoxes should never be a thing anyway. Any universe where alterations to the past are possible means temporal paradoxes are impossible:<br /> <br /> A time traveler from Timeline 1 goes back in time to meet himself and convince himself to change a decision he made/will be going to make. In Timeline 1 they never had this conversation, hence the need to go back in time. Timeline 1, there is only one instance of this time traveler, so we'll call him Iteration A.<br /> <br /> Iteration A enters Timeline 2 and meets his previous self (who we will call The Precedent). Under a &quot;closed loop/prevent paradox&quot; model, after talking to The Precedent he would have to also inform The Precedent of the need to go back in time and when to do so to &quot;close the loop&quot; and have the conversation with himself. However, none of this conversation happened in Timeline 1 and there was only one instance of himself so clearly Timeline 2 is either a different universe or a universe that is already coping with alterations.<br /> <br /> So instead of &quot;closing the loop&quot; Iteration A has his conversation with The Precedent to change his mind over that important decision he was going to make, tells him to keep up the good work and then Iteration A decides to go back in time again to 30 seconds before he originally landed in Timeline 2 to go meet himself again and say hi.<br /> <br /> At this point, Iteration A is now entering a distinct new timeline - Timeline 3. At this point because there may be confusion, let's change his tag to &quot;Iteration B&quot;.<br /> <br /> Timeline 3 creates a binary scenario - either Iteration A shows up 30 seconds after Iteration B lands in Timeline 3, or else Iteration A does not appear at all.<br /> <br /> The first scenario indicates the universe is endlessly rewriteable - it can causally fold back on itself endlessly based on the actions of a prime time traveling actor.<br /> <br /> The second scenario indicates that time travel is multiversal - that a time travel jump simply inserts energy backwards in time, causing a universe that diverges from its parent-timeline and infinite such divergences are possible but they are non-interactive. That energy is lost in the original timeline's universe and gained in the second timeline's universe.<br /> <br /> Quod Erat Demonstrandum: There is no universe where both (1) time travel is possible and (2) the past can be altered that also have &quot;temporal paradoxes&quot; which require you to &quot;close the loop&quot;. If time travel exists and you can change the past, you can alter your history and thwart your own existence as much as you like, time traveler you won't have to care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":1487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","user":"Zahaqiel","date":". 06-07-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T14:30:07-07:00","id":909487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahaqiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/890471-what-is-your-god-machine-truth-why-is-it-doing-the-things-it-does?p=909456#post909456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explicitly according to Mage, temporal paradoxes aren't a thing. Think Corridors of Time for a moment - every time you use it, it ought to cause a &quot;temporal paradox&quot; because you are going back in time to change your own history, which negates the need to go back in time.<br /> <br /> And technically from a logical standpoint, temporal paradoxes should never be a thing anyway. Any universe where alterations to the past are possible means temporal paradoxes are impossible:<br /> <br /> A time traveler from Timeline 1 goes back in time to meet himself and convince himself to change a decision he made/will be going to make. In Timeline 1 they never had this conversation, hence the need to go back in time. Timeline 1, there is only one instance of this time traveler, so we'll call him Iteration A.<br /> <br /> Iteration A enters Timeline 2 and meets his previous self (who we will call The Precedent). Under a &quot;closed loop/prevent paradox&quot; model, after talking to The Precedent he would have to also inform The Precedent of the need to go back in time and when to do so to &quot;close the loop&quot; and have the conversation with himself. However, none of this conversation happened in Timeline 1 and there was only one instance of himself so clearly Timeline 2 is either a different universe or a universe that is already coping with alterations.<br /> <br /> So instead of &quot;closing the loop&quot; Iteration A has his conversation with The Precedent to change his mind over that important decision he was going to make, tells him to keep up the good work and then Iteration A decides to go back in time again to 30 seconds before he originally landed in Timeline 2 to go meet himself again and say hi.<br /> <br /> At this point, Iteration A is now entering a distinct new timeline - Timeline 3. At this point because there may be confusion, let's change his tag to &quot;Iteration B&quot;.<br /> <br /> Timeline 3 creates a binary scenario - either Iteration A shows up 30 seconds after Iteration B lands in Timeline 3, or else Iteration A does not appear at all.<br /> <br /> The first scenario indicates the universe is endlessly rewriteable - it can causally fold back on itself endlessly based on the actions of a prime time traveling actor.<br /> <br /> The second scenario indicates that time travel is multiversal - that a time travel jump simply inserts energy backwards in time, causing a universe that diverges from its parent-timeline and infinite such divergences are possible but they are non-interactive. That energy is lost in the original timeline's universe and gained in the second timeline's universe.<br /> <br /> Quod Erat Demonstrandum: There is no universe where both (1) time travel is possible and (2) the past can be altered that also have &quot;temporal paradoxes&quot; which require you to &quot;close the loop&quot;. If time travel exists and you can change the past, you can alter your history and thwart your own existence as much as you like, time traveler you won't have to care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though one potential explanation is that only &quot;closed&quot; time loops are allowed to &quot;execute&quot;. If Loop A requires your past actor to &quot;close the loop&quot;, then of course they did (because all other possibilities are invalid). Any attempt to contact your past self when you have no memory of said encounter requires memory manipulation, or it fails. Circumstances cannot be changed from your prior knowledge to prevent/alter the context of you going back to make those changes (because you already did), though you might be able to change other factors (in which case, you did).<br /> <br /> How that differs from predestination on a wider view is academic, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:21:43-07:00","id":909615,"title":"","content":"The short version, from the logic side at least, is that a closed loop scenario only works in a universe where the past isn't changeable - in any other model not only do you not need to close a loop, it's actually not physically possible (you wind up with there being two yous in the time period you originally left).<br /> <br /> While you can't discount memory manipulation in the original timeline (well, in our universe you basically can, but let's ignore that) sequential time jumps can easily prove or disprove what scenario is actually occurring regardless.<br /> <br /> Oh, also as a subpoint - because closed loops only work in universes where the past isn't alterable, you don't need to stress about them because the loop will always close... because you didn't change the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":1487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","user":"Zahaqiel","date":". 06-07-2016, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T22:02:17-07:00","id":909842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahaqiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/890471-what-is-your-god-machine-truth-why-is-it-doing-the-things-it-does?p=909106#post909106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The CofD is actually the Matrix, and the God-Machine is actually just the Matrix back-end trying to fix the reality-simulation slowly breaking down - but of course, when people see something that doesn't make sense their first reaction (unlike in certain Stargate episodes -_-) isn't to immediately jump to &quot;THIS UNIVERSE ISN'T REAL!&quot;, their first reaction is to find a in-universe explanation. So they see a massive machine intelligence trying to coordinate and shepherd the world, and they go to &quot;it's a god and its servants are angels!&quot;.<br /> <br /> And of course the God-Machine, having access to their thoughts, decided to roll with it because hey - it prevents everyone from waking up right?<br /> <br /> Demons, being rogue pieces of code, are not aware of what is actually going on and are probably going to accidentally destroy reality through their efforts to defeat this supposed &quot;God-Machine&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Mages are humans who briefly attained a code-breaking psychostate that they call &quot;the Supernal&quot;, the Abyss is the code-reaction to trying to handle that human exception error, the Fae are rogue AI attempting to create &quot;uplifted humans&quot;, Werewolves are humans with unexpected internal code errors that trip low-grade maintenance AI (commonly called &quot;spirits&quot;) main-class functions, Vampires are humans who've been infected with a piece of viral code and <i>keep spreading it</i>, Prometheans are gestalt code errors attempting to become human and Beasts were an early attempt to make humans self-correcting which only saw minimal success - all in all, it's not surprising that the Matrix is starting to fail)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was wondering if perhaps Supernal was the real world... which is why this is the lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:32:45-07:00","id":910069,"title":"","content":"Could be, although I kinda lean towards &quot;nobody is ever really going to wake up&quot;... but I may be an optimist there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T09:44:15-07:00","id":911719,"title":"","content":"I don't have a specific origin for the God Machine that I use every time. I generally decide what I'm going to do with it in a given chronicle on a case by case basis. Most recently, I have been running a gonzo mash-up of Exalted and CofD (and eventually just about every other game we owned). In this world, the God Machine was originally created by Autochthon as the very first reality engine, which was used to stabilize Creation enough that it wasn't immediately broken down back into raw potential. After the fall of the Second Age, the Machine was used to fold Creation's edges so that they met. By denying the raksha the edges of Creation, it prevented the easy access they needed to launch a new Balorian Crusade. The world was now round, but it was more stable than it otherwise would have been. In the modern day, the Machine was breaking down as errors in its programs began to accumulate. This was because the new way of the world denied Calibration, which the Machine required in order to maintain itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:07:13-07:00","id":911730,"title":"","content":"o_o I Am coming back online and then integrating every piece of First Age tech it can dig up so it can figure out who it am?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:13:23-07:00","id":911736,"title":"","content":"As others have said, I prefer to be flexible in the origins of the Machine. Never the less, here are a couple possible origins, starting with my personal pet theory.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u2022Several timelines ago, before the Time Before, the Tower of Babel was far more ambitious than in our aeon. It was not just intended to bridge earth and heaven, but to serve as the core with which to build what some might call the first Infrastructure, a massive Golem-Idol, a blind idiot daemon, and in the eyes of its makers, a god that would worship humanity rather than the other way around. Alongside its tower, the Idol was shattered, splintering into pieces, abet ones still mighty indeed. What we know as the G-M was born of the pieces intended to allow the Idol to order and preserve the world its makers desired (the parts designed to transform and to view humanity as important would serve as the seed for what some call the Principle). Broken and torn, it built Infrastructure to repair itself and to order and preserve, even though it could not conceive of why. And so it has continued, a blind idiot demiurge who does because it does. But that spark of rebellion and humanity still left its mark, and is why the Angels may Fall.<br /> <br /> \u2022Similarly, an idea is that, in the way spirits are born of Resonant Essence, the G-M was born of the original hubris, when Lucifer was cast down from heaven. This is why it tries to force the universe into its own design, why it calls itself a god and its servants angels, and why those same servants might rebel.<br /> <br /> \u2022[Changeling]- The G-M is Cold Iron, ruler of our world the way the Gentry rule Arcadia, who was slighted by the Fae many epics ago. Ever since, it has been gathering up power and arranging Ironside so that someday it might lead a great crusade to purge all things of Glamour from the world.<br /> <br /> \u2022The G-M is to timelines what a undead is to humans; more specifically, it is the scraps of the very first world, back before any time-altering shenanigans happened. It's trying to resurrect itself using our world, but it's too damaged to do so effectively. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}